SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE
=====================

These terms cover the CODE in this repository and nothing else:

    scripts/    the build script, the pack importer, the travel-graph tooling
    src/        the map viewer/editor template
    tools/      the verification harness

They do NOT cover the map data, which sits under two separate regimes:

  - Zone geometry is traced by community map packs (such as Brewall's EverQuest
    maps). Those traces are their authors' work, not the licensor's, and are
    therefore not the licensor's to license. This repository does not
    redistribute them at all — they are converted from a pack you supply into a
    git-ignored cache on your own machine.

  - The authored layer under data/ describes EverQuest content. "EverQuest" and
    related zone and place names are trademarks of Daybreak Game Company LLC /
    Darkpaw Games, and EverQuest game content is their copyright. This project
    is unofficial and non-commercial, is not affiliated with or endorsed by
    Daybreak, and operates under fan-use tolerance rather than under any
    license granted by Daybreak.

A map you BUILD with this code embeds map geometry, and these terms do not
cover it. Where that geometry came from decides whose work it is:

  - Zones taken from a community map pack are that pack's authors' work,
    and this project claims no rights in them and passes none on.

  - Zones taken from the game client's own maps/ folder are Daybreak-authored
    files, and likewise not this project's to license.

A single built map can contain a mixture, and the conversion records which
layer supplied each zone — see rootZones and sources[].from in the generated
cache's manifest.json.

This project distributes the builder, which embeds no map geometry at all,
and additionally offers prebuilt maps as a convenience. Each prebuilt names
the source its geometry came from and credits that source's authors. That
credit is an attribution and not a license: this project asserts no ownership
of the underlying map data, and anyone redistributing a built map further
should confirm terms with the source it names.

See the "Data & attribution" section of README.md for the full picture. Not
legal advice.

The unmodified text of the license follows.

